// std.prelude — automatically imported symbols
//
// The prelude re-exports the most commonly used functions and types so that
// user code does not need explicit `use` statements for everyday operations.
//
// Currently all intrinsic functions are registered in the root scope by the
// compiler (see resolution::Resolver::register_intrinsic_functions), so this
// file serves as documentation and a future hook for the module system.

// ── I/O ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// print(value)       — print a value to stdout (no trailing newline)
// println(value)     — print a value to stdout followed by a newline

// ── Conversions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// to_i64(value)      — convert a value to i64
// to_f64(value)      — convert a value to f64
// to_string(value)   — convert a value to string

// ── Introspection ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// type_of(value)     — get the runtime type tag of a value

// ── Process ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// exit(code)         — terminate the process with exit code
// panic(message)     — abort with a panic message
